    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="1047" n="945" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg945"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-05-14T19:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Your 11, May 7, noon.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d814-f1"/> The Department
                    approached British Embassy on May 11 along lines suggested in your paragraph
                    4.</p>
                <p>Have you any mental reservations which would cause us to delay recognition? If
                    not, I purpose to request authority from the President to recognize the Barclay
                    régime shortly after you telegraph me that the Liberian Congress has withdrawn
                    its repudiationist legislation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
